# Secrets and local environment. Both halves of a server config are disclosure: tokens
# obviously, host inventories too. Neither ever lives in this tree.
.env
# Variants too: .env.local and .env.production are the same disclosure as .env, and only the
# bare name was covered. The two tracked .env.production files under oracles/ and tasks/ are
# ts-glob-hidden FIXTURES (that task is about globbing dotfiles), so they are re-included.
.env.*
!.env.example
!oracles/**/.env.production
!tasks/**/.env.production
*.secrets.json
pricing.json

# Agent session state, project-scoped MCP config and audit bookkeeping. Local to a machine,
# and on a developer box this can hold whole worktree checkouts.
.claude/

# Session scratch: one-off fix scripts and acceptance rigs. Durable guarantees belong in
# tests/, which is what a reader can run; nothing here is evidence of anything.
scratch/

# Run artifacts are published deliberately, per run, after review; work dirs never.
results/*/work/
# Working state from a prepare or ingest step: a rendered corpus, staged prompts, a pid and a
# stderr tail. None is evidence and `.prepare-feed/` holds a full corpus render, so a pathspec
# `git add results/` must not sweep them in.
results/.prepare-feed/
results/.ingest-staging/
results/.prepare-*.tgz
results/prepare.err
results/prepare.pid
staging/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
results/*/cfg/
results/*.log
results/*.err
results/*.pid
results/.ingest-staging/
results/*-staging/
results/*-tmp/
.claude/

# Assembled condition corpora: reproducible from the base corpus, plants.json and a seed.
corpus/conditions/
.venv-bench/
results/logs/

# Produced by `pip install -e .`, which is now possible. CI asserts a clean tree.
*.egg-info/

# Generated haystack corpora: reproducible from the generator digest, the scale and the seed.
# 25x is ~24 MB of transcripts, so the plan is the artefact and the corpus is rebuilt on demand.
corpus/haystack/

# Hugging Face payloads assembled by scripts/hf_stage.py. Reproducible from the tree and the
# two cards, and a staged copy that drifts from its source is worse than no copy at all.
build/
